+/-! ## Part 8: Strict Monotonicity and Acyclicity
+
+Descent chains have strictly decreasing objective values along every step.
+This implies acyclicity: no state can appear twice in a descent chain.
+-/
+
+/-
+**Strict f-decrease along descent chains.**
+For any two positions `i < j` in a descent chain, `f(x_j) < f(x_i)`.
+-/
+theorem descentChain_f_strictMono {d n : ℕ}
+    {S : Finset (Fin d → ℤ)} {f : (Fin d → ℤ) → ℤ}
+    (chain : DescentChain S f n)
+    {i j : Fin (n + 1)} (hij : i < j) :
+    f (chain.seq j) < f (chain.seq i) := by
+  induction' j using Fin.inductionOn with j ih;
+  · tauto;
+  · cases lt_or_eq_of_le ( show i ≤ Fin.castSucc j from Nat.le_of_lt_succ hij ) <;> simp_all +decide [ Fin.castSucc_lt_last ];
+    · exact lt_trans ( chain.step j |>.2.2.2 ) ih;
+    · exact chain.step j |>.2.2.2
+
+/-
+**Acyclicity of descent chains.**
+No point appears twice in a descent chain: if `chain.seq i = chain.seq j`
+and `i ≤ j`, then `i = j`.
+-/
+theorem descentChain_injective {d n : ℕ}
+    {S : Finset (Fin d → ℤ)} {f : (Fin d → ℤ) → ℤ}
+    (chain : DescentChain S f n) :
+    Function.Injective chain.seq := by
+  intro i j hij;
+  exact le_antisymm ( le_of_not_gt fun hi => by have := descentChain_f_strictMono chain hi; aesop ) ( le_of_not_gt fun hj => by have := descentChain_f_strictMono chain hj; aesop )
+
+/-
+**Descent chains are bounded by the cardinality of S.**
+Since descent chains are injective and map into `S`, the chain length
+cannot exceed `|S|`.
+-/
+theorem descentChain_length_le_card {d n : ℕ}
+    {S : Finset (Fin d → ℤ)} {f : (Fin d → ℤ) → ℤ}
+    (chain : DescentChain S f n) :
+    n + 1 ≤ S.card := by
+  convert Finset.card_le_card ( show Finset.image chain.seq Finset.univ ⊆ S from ?_ ) using 1;
+  · rw [ Finset.card_image_of_injective _ ( descentChain_injective chain ), Finset.card_fin ];
+  · exact Finset.image_subset_iff.mpr fun i _ => chain.mem i
+
+/-! ## Part 9: Depth Gap and Potential Interpolation
+
+The **depth gap** measures how much faster descent becomes at higher depth.
+This quantifies the interpolation between generic O(|S|) bounds and
+the tight O(D) bound at maximal depth.
+-/
+
+/-- **Depth gap ratio**: the factor by which a depth-k₂ bound improves over
+a depth-k₁ bound. Equal to `d^(k₂ - k₁)`. -/
+def depthGapRatio (d k₁ k₂ : ℕ) : ℚ :=
+  (d : ℚ) ^ (k₂ - k₁)
+
+/-
+The depth gap ratio is at least 1 when `k₁ ≤ k₂` and `d ≥ 1`.
+-/
+theorem depthGapRatio_ge_one {d k₁ k₂ : ℕ}
+    (hd : 1 ≤ d) (hk : k₁ ≤ k₂) :
+    1 ≤ depthGapRatio d k₁ k₂ := by
+  exact one_le_pow₀ ( mod_cast hd )
+
+/-
+**Quantitative improvement from deeper certificates.**
+The runtime bound at depth `k₂` is exactly `depthGapRatio d k₁ k₂` times
+better than at depth `k₁`.
+-/
+theorem depth_improvement_factor
+    {d k₁ k₂ : ℕ} {c C₀ : ℚ} {D : ℕ}
+    (hd : 1 ≤ d) (hk : k₁ ≤ k₂) (hk₂ : k₂ ≤ d) :
+    C₀ * ↑D * ↑d ^ (d - k₂) / c =
+    C₀ * ↑D * ↑d ^ (d - k₁) / c / depthGapRatio d k₁ k₂ := by
+  unfold depthGapRatio; ring;
+  rw [ show d - k₁ = ( d - k₂ ) + ( k₂ - k₁ ) by omega, pow_add ] ; ring;
+  simp +decide [ mul_comm, mul_left_comm, ne_of_gt ( zero_lt_one.trans_le hd ) ]
+
+/-! ## Part 10: Potential Strict Decrease Along Chains
+
+Strengthening of the telescoping decrease: the potential is strictly
+monotone along any descent chain, not just decreasing.
+-/
+
+/-
+**Strict potential decrease along chains.**
+For any valid descent chain with potential decrease `δ > 0`,
+the potential at step `j` is strictly less than at step `i` when `i < j`.
+-/
+theorem potential_strictMono_along_chain
+    (n : ℕ) (Φ : ℕ → ℚ) (δ : ℚ) (_hδ : 0 < δ)
+    (hdec : ∀ i, i < n → Φ (i + 1) + δ ≤ Φ i)
+    {i j : ℕ} (_hi : i ≤ n) (hj : j ≤ n) (hij : i < j) :
+    Φ j + (j - i : ℕ) * δ ≤ Φ i := by
+  induction hij <;> norm_num at *;
+  · exact hdec i hj;
+  · rename_i k hk₁ hk₂;
+    rw [ Nat.cast_sub ( by linarith ) ] at * ; push_cast at * ; nlinarith [ hdec k hj, hk₁ ( by linarith ) ]
+
 
